e most record highs of any decade (71). Parkersburg's all-time high is 104\u00b0F, on July 28, 1930.","t_chg":"Parkersburg's nights cooled over the long run. Its days have warmed since 1980.","p_chg":"Across 94 complete years: Parkersburg's average low has fallen <strong class='sig'>\u22120.08\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range \u22120.16 to \u22120.00), about \u22120.8\u00b0F since 1926. Parkersburg's average high shows no clear change: +0.03\u00b0F per decade, a range (\u22120.07 to +0.13) that includes zero. <strong>The last 40 years tell a different story:</strong> since 1980, lows show no clear change and highs have risen <strong class='sig'>+0.59\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.30 to +0.88). The full record joins different observing sites over the years, and a move (for example, from the city to a cooler airport) can hide or exaggerate a long-run trend, so the recent decades are the clearer guide here.","t_mon":"Lows rose in none; June fell. Highs rose in 2 of 12 months; January fell.","t_rain":"Parkersburg has gotten wetter","p_rain":"Parkersburg's yearly precipitation has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.55 inches per decade</strong> (95% range +0.08 to +1.03), about +5.5 inches since 1926. The 1991\u20132020 normal is 41.9 inches a year. The wettest year was 2011 (57.24 in); the driest, 1930 (19.70 in).","show_snow":true,"sig_bars":{"lo":false,"hi":false},"t_year":"2026 so far: 7 daily record highs, 5 daily record lows"}}